                <pb facs="0659" n="1619" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1619"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 129.—Note
                        verbale.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The ministry of foreign
                            affairs to the legation of the United
                            States.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sublime Porte,<lb/>Ministry of Foreign
                            Affairs</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 4,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In answer to the <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> that the legation of
                    the United States of America kindly addressed to the ministry of foreign affairs
                    on the 17th of May last (No. 27), the ministry of foreign affairs has the honor
                    to inform the United States legation that the measure concerning the Israelites
                    going to Palestine shall not be applied, except to those who emigrate in number
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">en nombre</hi>), and that no obstacle shall be
                    opposed to the sojourn of those who are not of this class.</p>
                <p>Instructions of this sense have already been sent to the governor of
                    Jerusalem.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
